# Rendered by the Akamas FileConfigurator task into params.env, then sourced by
# apply_config.sh -> render_statefulset.sh, which validates every value and writes the vLLM
# flags (booleans become --x / --no-x: vLLM 0.32.0 parses them with BooleanOptionalAction,
# vllm/engine/arg_utils.py get_kwargs, and rejects --x=true). Every flag below was checked
# against the v0.32.0 source (vllm/engine/arg_utils.py, vllm/config/{parallel,cache,scheduler}.py).
#
# EMPTY VALUE = FLAG OMITTED = vLLM's own default. Every key must be present (a missing line
# is refused), and a leftover ${...} token is refused (ignoreUnsubstitutedTokens false), but
# an empty value is legal: render_statefulset.sh then writes no flag and vLLM picks its
# default. The study itself always writes a value for every TUNED key (each step's values
# cover all of parametersSelection); empty values are for the FIXED keys at the bottom and
# for hand-made params.env files (calibration, smoke). Note that Akamas renders an empty
# string, not the token, for a parameter listed in a step's doNotRenderParameters.
#
# Topology (the pod always holds all four L4s, parity at 4 GPUs; parameterConstraints):
#   TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE x PREFILL_CONTEXT_PARALLEL_SIZE x DATA_PARALLEL_SIZE == 4.
#   DECODE_CONTEXT_PARALLEL_SIZE reuses the TP ranks (no extra GPUs): tp % dcp == 0
#   (vllm/config/parallel.py, the pcp == 1 branch); MLA has one KV head, so DCP up to TP
#   shards the latent KV cache instead of replicating it on every TP rank (KV x2 at DCP2,
#   x4 at DCP4: 374,192 -> 724,800 -> 1,524,864 tokens measured at gmu 0.90).
#   PCP > 1 needs DCP 1 for this model (v1/worker/gpu/pcp_manager.py: "MRV2 PCP + DCP
#   supports sparse MLA models only"; DeepSeek-V2-Lite is dense MLA), EP on (TP2xPCP2 without
#   EP crashed in the smoke run: topk_softmax is_padding size mismatch) and DP 1 (PCP + DP
#   unverified). render_statefulset.sh refuses every combination the study's
#   parameterConstraints exclude, so a hand-made params.env cannot slip past them.
# ENABLE_EXPERT_PARALLEL: true/false. Without EP the experts are TP-sharded across all
#   dp x pcp x tp ranks (model_executor/layers/fused_moe/config.py, flatten_tp_across_dp_and_pcp);
#   with EP each rank holds 64/ranks whole experts.
# KV_CACHE_DTYPE: auto (bf16) or fp8. TRITON_MLA (the decode backend selected on SM 8.9)
#   lists fp8 / fp8_e4m3 in supported_kv_cache_dtypes and needs SM89+ for native fp8 (L4 is
#   SM 8.9). fp8 with PCP (FlashAttention MLA prefill) is unverified.
# MAX_NUM_SEQS / MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS: vLLM 0.32.0 GPU defaults for the OpenAI server on a
#   device under 70 GiB (L4 = 24 GB): 256 / 2048 (arg_utils.py get_batch_defaults), per
#   engine (DP4 = four schedulers). scheduler.py raises if max_num_batched_tokens < max_num_seqs.
# GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION: 0.90 baseline (repo convention; vLLM default 0.92). 31.4 GB of
#   bf16 weights over 4 x 22.5 GiB usable leaves ~10.8 GiB of KV per GPU at TP4 (measured).
TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE=${vllm.tensor_parallel_size}
DATA_PARALLEL_SIZE=${vllm.data_parallel_size}
DECODE_CONTEXT_PARALLEL_SIZE=${vllm.decode_context_parallel_size}
PREFILL_CONTEXT_PARALLEL_SIZE=${vllm.prefill_context_parallel_size}
ENABLE_EXPERT_PARALLEL=${vllm.enable_expert_parallel}
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=
MAX_NUM_SEQS=${vllm.max_num_seqs}
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=${vllm.max_num_batched_tokens}
GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=${vllm.gpu_memory_utilization}
# --- Fixed, not tuned (empty = vLLM default) ---
# ENABLE_PREFIX_CACHING: empty = vLLM's default (on for this model). DCP/PCP together with
#   prefix caching is UNVERIFIED (the smoke run had it off): the calibration run checks it
#   (README "Before starting"); if a layout fails with it on, set false here and document it.
ENABLE_PREFIX_CACHING=
